yes. you use exactly the same syntax as the one you use to call another 
function.

> By User defined I mean, say I write a function to perform some
> calculations and display plots from the given data.
>
> Am I supposed to place the function in some particular place for R to
> know that there is this particular function.

The easiest is to place it in the global environment, so if your code is 
defined in foo.R, then just source foo.R .

r.eval( " source('foo.R') " ) ;

Otherwise, make a package out of your functions and load the package.

