Yes, those exist in the REngine API which is a high-level API that can  
handle different engines including JRI and Rserve. It is recommended  
over the low-level JRI/RNI API. See
http://rforge.net/org/docs/org/rosuda/REngine/package-summary.html

The REngine is now part of rJava distribution so you'll find it in the  
jri directory.

